* ============================================================================
* workspace_ram_hydrate.dts -- memo -> RAM hydration (owner lane step 2,
* 2026-08-11): WORKSPACE LOAD <name> MEMO RAM copies the posture's tables and
* native CDX files from their DISK homes into the mounted RAM VFS (through
* xbase::ramfs streams -- never std::filesystem, which would land on real
* disk while claiming RAM), then loads the posture with its roots re-pointed
* at RAM via the DTSHEMA 3 self-location mechanism. LMDB is not hydrated
* (owner rule "lmdb only for disks"; ramfs.hpp: LMDB must mmap a real OS
* file). Memo-sidecar hydration is chartered with the Part B regeneration
* (no MCC table carries a memo field yet).
*
* The hydration is TIMED and prints a measured line -- first measure
* 2026-08-11 (build 14:59:07): 24 file(s), 92139 B in 94.2 ms, and the VDISK
* census independently agreed byte-for-byte (92139 B / 24 files).
*
* Self-contained: saves its own v3 source posture from mcc_x64 first, so it
* never depends on hand-made catalog rows. VDISK UNMOUNT at the end is the
* DISMISS exit of the two-exit close: all RAM files dropped, disk untouched.
*
* Run: DO workspace_ram_hydrate  |  regression: REGRESSION RUN WORKSPACE_RAM
* Markers: HYD_T1 (STUDENTS row readable from the RAM-resident copy).
* ============================================================================
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

FORMULA "WS-RAM-HYDRATE-BEGIN"

* --- author the source posture (v3, self-locating) from the disk env --------
SETPATH DBF DBF/X64
SETPATH INDEXES INDEXES/X64
WORKSPACE CLOSE
WORKSPACE LOAD mcc_x64
WORKSPACE SAVE ram_hydrate_src MEMO V3
WORKSPACE CLOSE

* --- mount the RAM VFS and hydrate ------------------------------------------
DO mem
WORKSPACE LOAD ram_hydrate_src MEMO RAM

* --- residency + readability proof ------------------------------------------
VDISK STATUS
SELECT 8
TOP
? "HYD_T1_students_in_ram:" + (SID >= 1)

FORMULA "WS-RAM-HYDRATE-END"

* --- the dismiss exit: drop everything, restore the disk environment --------
WORKSPACE CLOSE
VDISK UNMOUNT
DO x64
